Output produced with these weights for a non-commercial purpose is yours.


3. WHY -- AND WHAT WOULD CHANGE IT
----------------------------------
These weights were trained on a mixed corpus:

  Poly Haven HDRIs          CC0                    no restriction
                            https://polyhaven.com/license

  HdM-HDR-2014              free for ACADEMIC and educational use;
  HdM-HFR-2017              COMMERCIAL use requires a separate agreement
                            with Hochschule der Medien Stuttgart
                            https://hdm-stuttgart.de/vmlab/hdm-hdr-2014/

  Netflix Chimera           CC BY 4.0 -- requires attribution
                            https://opencontent.netflix.com/

  FXTD Studios footage      proprietary, FXTD's own

The HdM term is the binding one. It is a contract accepted at download, not
only a copyright question, so it holds regardless of how the unsettled
question of whether trained weights are a derivative work of their training
data is eventually answered. FXTD Studios cannot waive somebody else's term,
so it does not pretend to: the licence above is narrower than what FXTD
alone could grant.

`pipeline/render_hdri_moves.py` builds training pairs from the CC0 Poly Haven
panoramas alone. Weights retrained on CC0 material plus FXTD's own footage
carry no upstream condition, and are intended to be released under Apache 2.0
as an unrestricted replacement for these. See STATUS.md.


